# Build verification output (dist-offline-* / dist-release-* etc.).
#   2026-10-28: packaging checks left dist-offline-verification-20261028/ (321 MiB)
#   and dist-release-verification-20261028/ (660 MiB) untracked at repo root.
#   A careless `git add .` would commit an Electron runtime; once pushed those
#   blobs stay in history forever. Block it at the source.
#
#   Three points, all measured on git 2.56.0:
#     1. The leading slash is required: `dist-*/` also ignores same-named
#        directories in SUBdirectories (sub/dist-bbb was ignored), while
#        `/dist-*/` applies to the repo root only (sub/dist-bbb stays visible).
#     2. The trailing slash limits the match to directories, so a plain file
#        with the same name is not affected.
#     3. This rule only hides these directories from `git status`; it does NOT
#        free disk space. Deleting them is a separate destructive action.
#
#   Complementary to `dist/` above, not a replacement: `/dist-*/` matches only
#   names starting with `dist-` and does not cover `dist/` itself. Keep both.
/dist-*/
build/
.cache/
*.zip

